        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "14 Dun Coran, Sweetfields, Youghal, Co. Cork, P36 F785\r\n\r\nDNG Spillane are delighted to present 14 Dun Coran, Sweetfields to the market, an exceptionally well-presented three-bedroom semi-detached residence enjoying a particularly generous site within this established and highly convenient residential development.\r\n\r\nExtending to approximately 100 m², the property is presented in very good condition throughout and offers well-proportioned accommodation ideally suited to modern family living. In addition to the principal accommodation, the property has the considerable benefit of a converted attic accessed via a permanent staircase, together with a substantially larger rear garden than is typically found within the development.\r\n\r\nInternally, the house has been finished and maintained to a very good standard, with a bright and welcoming feel throughout. The ground floor provides comfortable and practical living accommodation, with a well-proportioned living room complemented by a spacious kitchen/dining area overlooking and providing access to the rear garden.\r\n\r\nAt first-floor level, there are three bedrooms, including a main bedroom with en-suite, together with a family bathroom. The accommodation is well balanced, providing excellent bedroom space while retaining the practicality required for day-to-day family life.\r\n\r\nA permanent staircase continues from the first floor to the converted attic, which is one of the property's most useful additional features. This substantial space offers considerable flexibility and is ideally suited for use as a games room, home office, hobby room or additional storage space. While the attic is not included within the stated 100 m² floor area due to ceiling-height requirements, it provides a valuable additional level of usable space and considerably enhances the overall versatility of the property.\r\n\r\nExternally, No. 14 is particularly impressive. The rear garden is significantly larger than those typically associated with properties within Dun Coran and is a genuine feature of the home. Its generous proportions provide excellent space for children, outdoor dining, entertaining and gardening, while also offering a level of outdoor space that can be difficult to find in a modern residential development.\r\n\r\nA further benefit is the substantial Steeltech shed positioned within the rear garden. Complete with both electricity and plumbing, it offers excellent storage and additional practical space with the flexibility to accommodate a range of uses.\r\n\r\nOff-street parking is provided to the front of the property, while oil-fired central heating serves the accommodation.\r\n\r\nThe location further enhances the appeal of No. 14. Dun Coran is conveniently situated within easy reach of Youghal town centre and its excellent selection of shops, schools, cafés, restaurants and everyday amenities. The area is also renowned for its coastline, with a choice of beaches and recreational amenities readily accessible from the property.\r\n\r\nFor those commuting further afield, Cork City is approximately 40 minutes away, allowing purchasers to enjoy the benefits of coastal living while retaining excellent accessibility to the city and the wider East Cork region.\r\n\r\n14 Dun Coran is a particularly appealing family home that stands out for the quality of its presentation, generous accommodation and, importantly, the additional space it provides both internally and externally. The combination of a converted attic, an exceptionally large rear garden and a fully serviced Steeltech shed makes this a highly versatile property in a convenient Youghal location.\r\n\r\nViewing is highly recommended and strictly by appointment with sole selling agents DNG Spillane."
